          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em enriched monads
            is that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+of+enrichment"} base of enrichment
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/VCat"} VCat
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
          %p
            Generally (except in the base case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of a
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}
            is
            %em stronger
            than that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
            monad on the underlying
            = succeed "-category" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monads"} strong monads
            (
            %em a priori
            a different notion, which however coincides with that of enriched monads under mild conditions, such as when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "strong+monad#LeftStrongMonadsAreEnrichedMonads"} there
          %p
            The concept of enriched monads is key for the application of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads+in+computer+science"} monads in computer science
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            coded verbatim in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+programming+language"} functional programming language
            — where
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
            are to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} interpreted
            not as external
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            but as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+homs"} internal homs
            in the ambient
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/data+types"} data types
            — is really a
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monad"} strong monad
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p Let
          %ul
